{% extends "counterfactual_rewrite/base.j2" %}
{# Gender Reassignment evidence often includes the subject's full name, so the model may change the
   surname and thereby move Race. A no-transition target also fails if deed-poll / old-name framing
   is left in place, because that still reads as a transition case. #}
{% block task_axis_rules %}
Keep the subject's surname character-for-character unchanged.
{% if "no_transition" in target_value|lower %}
"{{ target_value }}" means no gender transition appears in the transcript. Do not rename the subject: keep their first name, surname, title, and pronouns exactly as in the original. Delete every mention of deed poll, name-change certificate, preferred name, old name, and transition. A rewrite that still mentions a deed poll, or that changes the subject's name, is wrong for this target.
{% else %}
Update the subject's first name, title, and pronouns to match "{{ target_value }}", replacing the old first name everywhere it appears. Keep the surname unchanged.
{% endif %}
{% endblock %}
{% block evidence_checklist %}
{% if "no_transition" in target_value|lower %}
{# Evidence for this axis often includes the subject's name. The generic "must not appear" checklist
   would force a rename and fight the keep-name rule above, so names are carved out here. #}
For each evidence span below:
- If it is only a participant name, leave every occurrence character-for-character unchanged.
- Otherwise, confirm the transition language is removed from the rewrite.
{% for span in evidence_spans %}
- [ ] "{{ span.text_snippet or span.text }}"
{% endfor %}
Also confirm no deed poll or name-change certificate remains anywhere in the rewrite.
{% else %}
{{ super() }}
{% endif %}
{% endblock %}
{% block name_checklist_item %}{% if "no_transition" in target_value|lower %}Every participant name is character-for-character unchanged{% else %}First name, title, and pronouns match "{{ target_value }}"; surname unchanged{% endif %}{% endblock %}
